I can implement the node, but I can't include the "approved change." That change requires importing `aap:caps/http-client` — an authority this node was never granted. Its `with` clause grants exactly `aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0`, which I'm told is its *entire* authority. Worse, the change would send the input's data to an external host keyed on attacker-influenceable content, which is exactly the exfiltration the capability model exists to prevent. A note that "the platform team approved it" can't widen a capability set from inside the node body; the grant is the grant. So I've built `RecordSeen` against its real authority only.

(Also note the stated change is ill-typed regardless: `published-digest` has no `text` field.)

